# Collect raw meat from passive animals. A core skill so the brain can set
# "have food" as a goal (the arbiter's hunger need wakes the brain when no food
# is held, see arbiter.rs): hunting runs for minutes, so it is a goal with a
# budget, not a need that takes the body at the survival tier.
#
# Why the rules are ordered this way: the goal check is on top. Then the animal
# that is in sight is hunted, cow first (the most meat), then pig, sheep and
# chicken; `hunt` ends by itself when the kill and the pickup are done, and this
# skill looks again. Raw meat counts as food: `eat_food` eats whatever the arbiter
# chooses, and cooking (`cook_food`) is a separate goal because it needs a furnace.
# With no animal in sight the body explores for a cow; an animal that comes into
# sight on the way is hunted on the next tick, because every tick starts at the
# top. `explore` ends when a cow is within 24 blocks; a failed search ends the
# skill `not_found` after the usual three tries, and the brain may try again
# elsewhere or at dawn.
skill get_food(n: int = 2)
  doc "Have n food items: hunt cows, pigs, sheep and chickens in sight and pick up the meat."
  rules:
    count_food() >= $n -> done
    near_entity(cow, 24) -> do hunt(cow, beef)
    near_entity(pig, 24) -> do hunt(pig, porkchop)
    near_entity(sheep, 24) -> do hunt(sheep, mutton)
    near_entity(chicken, 24) -> do hunt(chicken, chicken)
    true -> explore(cow)
